# Manim writes everything it generates under media/: rendered scenes, the
# LaTeX and Text glyph caches, section files, partial movie files, and the
# text-to-speech cache. All of it is reproducible from source, and the partial
# movie files alone run to hundreds of megabytes per chapter.
media/

# Chapter masters used to land in videos/ under manimgl. Ignored so an old
# working copy does not start committing 180 MB of renders after a pull.
videos/

# manim-slides writes its per-scene slide-break metadata and concatenated
# clip cache here, relative to wherever it was invoked from -- reproducible
# from source the same way media/ is.
slides/

# Secrets. .env holds ELEVEN_API_KEY; .env.example is the tracked template.
.env
!.env.example

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
